# Casa de los Motes (the name changer's house, name changer; F2, contract 74; map id 178), 9 x 7, interior. column = i, row = j. A quiet scholar's room lined with books of names: four shelves, candles, a table with a quill and a rug.
# The Nombrador renames a creature of yours with the naming keyboard (`nick_prompt`: the question, then the keyboard), but only one you are the ORIGINAL TRAINER of: one that arrived over the IR link is refused (`bond ot`, Mon.xf MX_TRADED).
@map casa_motes
@size 9 7
@interior yes
@bg 3
@fill floor_wood
@spawn door 4 5 N
@var mt_slot 5
@var mt_ot 6
@legend
  .  tile=floor_wood
  C  tile=none object=wall_corner
  w  tile=none object=wall_j
  y  tile=none object=wall_win_j
  |  tile=none object=wall_i
  q  tile=none object=wall_win_i
  B  object=bookshelf interact=look text=motes.books
  K  object=bookshelf interact=look text=casa.books
  c  object=candle_s
  T  object=table
  P  object=planter
  N  npc=psiquico_s id=namer face=SW script=namer
  m  tile=mat
@grid
  Cwwywwyww
  |BKBcKB..
  |...N...P
  |.....T..
  q.c......
  |........
  |...mm...
@warp m -> ciudad_nodo spawn=motes_door
# The Nombrador: the party list picks the creature; `bond ot` says whether it is the player's own (1) or an IR-traded one (0); then `nick_prompt SLOT` (it takes the slot as an immediate, hence the six branches) asks and opens the keyboard.
@script namer npc
    npc_face_hero namer
    say motes.hi
    ask motes.ask
    jv 0 1 go
    say motes.no
    end
  go:
    say motes.which
    pick_party mt_slot
    jv mt_slot 255 no
    bond ot mt_slot
    jv mt_ot 1 mine
    say motes.traded
    end
  no:
    say motes.no
    end
  mine:
    jv mt_slot 0 s0
    jv mt_slot 1 s1
    jv mt_slot 2 s2
    jv mt_slot 3 s3
    jv mt_slot 4 s4
    nick_prompt 5
    jmp done
  s0:
    nick_prompt 0
    jmp done
  s1:
    nick_prompt 1
    jmp done
  s2:
    nick_prompt 2
    jmp done
  s3:
    nick_prompt 3
    jmp done
  s4:
    nick_prompt 4
  done:
    say motes.done
@end
